{"user": "At the end, playing a1 then h1 flipped almost the whole top row. Was there any risk White could have replied to one of those?", "user_ts": "2026-08-12T21:47:51.490072+00:00", "assistant": "No real risk **if the game let you play a1 then h1 back-to-back**.\n\nIn Othello, White only gets skipped if White has **no legal move** and must pass. So after your **a1**, if White didn\u2019t move before your **h1**, that means **White had no legal reply at all**.\n\nAnd once you took **both corners**, the top row became effectively locked: corner discs can\u2019t be flipped, and the row between them was stable. So White couldn\u2019t \u201cundo\u201d that sweep afterward.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-12T21:47:51.490072+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-12T21:47:56.490072+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 3, "Common Ground Question": 1, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 2}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 1.0, "Common Ground Question": 0.3333333333333333, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "llama": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Local Justification": 3, "Worked Line": 1, "General Principle": 3, "Neutral Feedback": 1}, "confidence": {"Local Justification": 1.0, "Worked Line": 0.3333333333333333, "General Principle": 1.0, "Neutral Feedback": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Local Justification", "Worked Line", "General Principle"], "llama": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"], "sonnet": ["Local Justification", "General